<p>I was really, really into this from the start. It's a great premise, and the introduction of the doors gave me some strong 093 vibes - I was very excited to see how each exploration segued together and to explore the story world.</p>
<p>Unfortunately, I wasn't really able to get into it. The dialogue from the researcher and the notation regarding audio felt far too leading at times, taking away from atmosphere by way of tell over show and robbing me of the ability to really envision the setting without a ton of hand-holding.</p>
<p>Also, I'll admit I'm missing the significance of the alt-u's AICs acting up, how does that relate to anything? And further questioning if TSAT is supposed to have been similarly affected - if not, seems like a missed opportunity.</p>

